WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.900
<v Mike>Jackie Chan's Action Kung Fu!

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.500
<v Mike>Jackie and his sister Josephine are tough on tyrants.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.360
<v Mike>And welcome to NEStalgia!

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.720
<v Mike>A chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.980
<v Hosts>I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.220
<v Hosts>And I'm Joe.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.760
<v Mike>Okay, first off, Jackie Chan does not have a sister named Josephine.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.420
<v Joe>I was Googling it right this moment.

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.080
<v Joe>I was like, does he really have a sister?

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.820
<v Mike>He has two half-siblings.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.440
<v Sean>Or either of them Josephine.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.100
<v Mike>I don't even think he knew.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.220
<v Mike>No, they are not.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:53.880
<v Mike>And I don't think he knew either of his half-siblings until after this game came out.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.560
<v Sean>So there's some kind of like family drama that we haven't gotten like privy to.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:03.980
<v Mike>Right. But it just begs the question, how involved can Jackie Chan be if they're also just like making

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:04.800
<v Sean>up his sister?

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.060
<v Mike>He wouldn't have agreed to that, right?

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.380
<v Mike>I don't know. Why not?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.400
<v Joe>If he didn't know about his real siblings, why not?

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.080
<v Joe>I'd say that if- Maybe he's always wanted a sibling.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.420
<v Sean>Yeah. If you're making a game about me, I say have at it.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:24.180
<v Mike>Give me siblings. Because I was thinking maybe it was like pitched originally as like, oh, this is the princess.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.560
<v Mike>And he was like, no, I don't do that.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:28.480
<v Mike>You know, like I don't, I'm an eligible guy.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.240
<v Sean>I need to be related. Right, right.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.300
<v Mike>Yeah. I wanted to be my sister, I say.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.480
<v Mike>Also, tough on tyrants.

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.880
<v Mike>Is that really like a stance?

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.040
<v Mike>Does anyone not have that stance in life?

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.620
<v Mike>Like, is that really a core value?

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.040
<v Sean>Yeah. Tyrants probably don't.

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.760
<v Mike>That's true. But they don't know that they're the tyrants.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.400
<v Mike>I guess that's the problem with the world.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:56.080
<v Mike>Huh. Yeah. By the time this game hit in 1990, Jackie Chan was a gigantic star in Hong Kong, but didn't

00:01:56.080 --> 00:02:00.860
